{
  "_doc": [
    "Shared test vectors of the graph v1 sanitizer (contracts.md section 7, red team #14). The backend (services/auth/fs-template-graph.js, CommonJS) and the core",
    "(src/board-template-graph.js, ESM) must give the SAME answer for every case: copy this file into the core (src/graph-v1-vectors.json) and read it in both tests.",
    "Each case: { name, input, expect }. `input` is passed to cleanGraph(input) with keepMedia = false (the sharing path; the core's keepMedia:true path is tested on its own).",
    "`expect` is { ok:true, nodes, wires, dropped } or { ok:false, reason }. Key order inside objects does not matter; array order does.",
    "Count limits (more than 100 nodes, more than 300 wires), the 64 KB output size and long strings (cut to the key's maximum) are generated in code by each test, not stored here.",
    "Rules in short: unknown node types are dropped and counted in `dropped` (wires on them go too, indexes are renumbered); wire from/to must be integers in range; a handle that is",
    "present but not a safe id drops the wire; strings lose control characters except \\n \\t and lone surrogates; numbers are rounded and clamped to +-1e6; values outside the allowlist",
    "are dropped from `data` (the receiver falls back to its default)."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "text: keeps content and _title, rounds the position, drops every other key",
      "input": { "nodes": [ { "type": "text", "position": { "x": 10.4, "y": -20.6 }, "data": { "content": "Hello", "_title": "Intro", "handle": "h1", "url": "fs-media://pick/abc", "task_id": "t1", "path": "/etc/passwd", "evil": { "a": 1 } } } ], "wires": [] },
      "expect": { "ok": true, "nodes": [ { "type": "text", "position": { "x": 10, "y": -21 }, "data": { "content": "Hello", "_title": "Intro" } } ], "wires": [], "dropped": 0 }
    },
    {
